  "notes": "GAAP-format city statements. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); business-type from the proprietary funds Total column (p6), interest expense included in disbursements. The only supplementary schedule (p8, an all-funds budgetary schedule mistakenly titled 'Village of Paxton' but with Hay Springs' figures) is a combined all-funds schedule, so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (General, Street) and proprietary funds statement (Water, Sewer, RV Park), per the user's per-fund rule. Ending cash = governmental funds balance sheet cash held by County Treasurer 3,859; certificates of deposit 42,070 as ending_investments; the governmental funds also carry a cash deficit liability 105,154. Business-type disbursements reported total = Statement of Activities business-type expenses 219,879 (p2). Several printed totals are off by 1 (rounding), recorded in report_discrepancies. Read pages 1-8 of 8"
